n: 3.14
name: ice-water-gas-origin
kind: hub
is: The three words first appear on the disk in the first commit of the Living Codex, 2025-09-09: ice is essential persisted facts, water materialized caches, gas derivable or transient, with compiled code as gas. NUMS.Go has none of the words. The reading counts 21 uses on 12 axes: 12 compatible, 5 conflicting, 4 loose. The owner rejected the binding of state to kind on 2026-06-08. No definition by the owner was found, only short statements. The reading proposes state as the reach of a node's commitment, three invariants and six operations.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.14.1
name: origin
kind: hub
is: The oldest definition on the disk is the Living Codex of September 2025, committed under the owner's name with no assistant trailer: a state field on every node, ice kept small, the spec as ice and compiled code as gas, and code that refuses illegal moves. Its melt edits a node under the same id, and the older foundation document its spec cites is not on the disk.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.14.1.1
name: oldest-definition
kind: observation
is: The oldest use on the disk is commit 5fc24ba of the Living Codex, 2025-09-09, the repository's first. Line 24 of its spec reads: "Ice = essential persisted facts (atoms, deltas). Water = materialized caches/prototypes. Gas = derivable/transient." The same commit holds the enum ContentState { Ice, Water, Gas }.
status: observed
src: 2.22.3#24 2.22.2#commit-5fc24ba
limit: The spec says it is aligned to a "Living Codex - Self-Reflexive Foundation 4.1" whose section 4 was titled "Lenses (Ice/Water/Gas)" (lines 346 and 356); that document is not on the disk.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.14.1.2
