n: 3.14.1.4
name: enforcing-machinery
kind: observation
is: The Living Codex head enforces the states in code. The phase module refuses to melt a node that is not ice and to refreeze one that is not water. Ice is stored in PostgreSQL, water in SQLite, gas is not persisted. An edge takes the more fluid state of its two endpoints, with eight tests. An audit module moves regenerable nodes from ice to water.
status: observed
src: 2.22.7#60,75-78,135,150-153 2.22.8#9-14,444-457 2.22.9#40,66,92,118,149,184,220,256 2.22.10#11-12 2.22.11#19-21
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.14.2
name: later-uses
kind: hub
is: From February to November 2026 the three words were reused on further axes, almost all in assistant-written text, among them: pipeline stage, idea lifecycle, kind of node, settledness read from counts, what crosses between runtimes, JIT form, cache tier, lexicon maturity, queue pressure, compiled image on disk, and home of the node population. NUMS.Go and the five axioms contain none of the three words. The 2026-11-05 carrier has freeze and thaw without them.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.14.2.3
name: application-lifecycle-uses
kind: observation
is: In the parent repository's application the words name an idea's lifecycle: gas is ideation, ice is "frozen potential, not yet implemented", water is "being implemented, run, or used". Another service there calls a spec ice once it has actual_value > 0 and a non-empty implementation summary. The application's node model has a phase column defaulting to water, so the words are applied to every node of its graph with the stage of an idea as their meaning. A sibling repository's spec of 2026-02-12 names six transitions, with sublimation and deposition.
status: observed
src: 2.22.14#123-134 2.22.15#1-4,22-36 2.22.12#38-71
limit: All three files are assistant text.
at: 2026-11-24

